WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.322
Security controls need visibility.

2
00:00:02.322 --> 00:00:17.687
If authentication fails repeatedly, authorization denies an unexpected pattern, configuration fails validation, exceptions rise after deployment, or administrative settings change, the team needs enough signal to investigate.

3
00:00:17.687 --> 00:00:23.833
Logging and monitoring are what turn security design into something operators can observe.

4
00:00:23.833 --> 00:00:39.949
Useful events include authentication failures, authorization denials, suspicious request patterns, unusual exception trends, configuration problems, high-impact administrative changes, sensitive export activity, and dependency failures.

5
00:00:39.949 --> 00:00:49.714
Structured logging and correlation identifiers help connect events across middleware, endpoints, services, background work, and infrastructure.

6
00:00:49.714 --> 00:00:55.860
Safe logging means recording useful context without creating another sensitive data store.

7
00:00:55.860 --> 00:01:03.986
Logs should avoid secrets, tokens, passwords, raw sensitive request data, private records, and excessive personal data.

8
00:01:03.986 --> 00:01:12.659
Prefer safe identifiers, route patterns, operation names, outcomes, status categories, correlation IDs, and failure categories.

9
00:01:12.659 --> 00:01:16.551
Production readiness includes more than application code.

10
00:01:16.551 --> 00:01:33.828
Review dependency updates, secure headers and configuration, environment settings, secret rotation plans, Data Protection key storage, backup and restore expectations, incident response handoff, health checks, logging access, and operational dashboards.

11
00:01:33.828 --> 00:01:35.194
A secure ASP.

12
00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:39.974
NET Core application must be deployable, observable, and maintainable.

13
00:01:39.974 --> 00:01:45.437
Monitoring should focus on meaningful patterns rather than every isolated event.

14
00:01:45.437 --> 00:01:48.306
Alert fatigue makes teams less responsive.

15
00:01:48.306 --> 00:01:55.681
Tune thresholds, ownership, routing, and runbooks so alerts reach the right team with enough context to act.

16
00:01:55.681 --> 00:02:00.597
After incidents or missed signals, improve logs, metrics, and playbooks.
